    "markdown": "---\ntitle: \"Blera fallax\"\nsubtitle: \"(Linnaeus, 1758)\"\nparams:\n  species: \"Blera fallax\"\ninclude-in-header:\n  - text: |\n      <style>\n      #title-block-header .title{\n          text-align:center;\n          font-size:3rem;\n          font-style:italic;\n          font-family:Georgia, \"Times New Roman\", serif;\n          color:#000;\n          margin-bottom: 10rem !important;\n          margin-top: 3rem !important;\n      }\n      </style>\n---\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n:::\n\n\n### Author {.author-species}\n\nHinatea Ariey\n\n::: {.columns}\n\n::: {.column width=\"50%\" }\n\n\n<div class=\"dropdown\" id=\"menu-ids\">\n<button class=\"dropdown-btn\" onclick=\"document.getElementById('menu-ids').classList.toggle('open')\">Synonyms ▾</button>\n<div class=\"dropdown-content scroller\">\n<span>Musca fallax Linnaeus, 1758</span>\n<span>Blera nipponica Shiraki, 1968</span>\n<span>Cynorrhina fallax</span>\n<span>Musca ruficaudis De Geer, 1776</span>\n<span>Syrphus seminiger Panzer, 1804</span>\n<span>Syrphus semirufus Fabricius, 1794</span>\n<span>Blera nipponica Shiraki, 1968</span>\n<span>Cynorrhina fallax</span>\n<span>Musca ruficaudis De Geer, 1776</span>\n<span>Syrphus seminiger Panzer, 1804</span>\n<span>Syrphus semirufus Fabricius, 1794</span>\n</div>\n</div>\n::: {.species-taxonomy}\n**Subfamily** *Eristalinae* &nbsp; **Tribe** *Milesiini*\n:::\n::: {.species-common-names}\n**EN** &nbsp;   Pine Hoverfly<br>\n**LB** &nbsp;   Blera fallax<br>\n**FR** &nbsp;   Blera fallax<br>\n**DE** &nbsp;   Hundeschnauzenschwebfliege<br>\n:::\n:::\n\n\n::: {.column width=\"50%\"}\n\n\n## Conservation status {.no-top-margin}\n::: {.columns .status-row}\n\n::: {.column width=\"25%\"}\n### Europe\n:::\n::: {.column width=\"25%\"}\n![](/images/LC.png){.logo}\n:::\n:::\n\n::: {.columns .status-row}\n\n::: {.column width=\"50%\"}\n### European Union<br>(27)\n:::\n::: {.column width=\"50%\"}\n![](/images/LC.png){.logo}\n:::\n:::\n\n::: {.columns .status-row}\n\n::: {.column width=\"25%\"}\n### Luxembourg  (preliminary)\n:::\n::: {.column width=\"25%\"}\n![](/images/NTLU.png){.logo}\n:::\n:::\n\n:::\n:::\n\n\n![](/images/blera_fallax.jpg){.species-photo}\n\n## Activity period\n\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n![](blera_fallax_files/figure-html/g-source-1.png){width=864}\n:::\n:::\n\n## Description\n\nA medium hoverfly with an unmistakable pattern of coloration. Head, thorax and the upper part of abdomen black, the rest of the body is orange. Proportion of the orange part may varies depending on the sex, it should be bigger and clearer in males. Antenna on a protrusion of the front, face yellow [@bot2023].\n\n## Habitat\n### Immature\n\nLarva can be found in cavities in coniferous trees [@bot2023].\n\n### Mature\n\nAs the larva stage, adult affectioned spruce and pine forest with overmature trees but can also be observed in mixed forest [@speight2017; @bot2023].\n\n## Distribution\n\nLocalised in coniferous area, this syrphid can be found all around Luxembourg if the habitat is suitable.\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n\n```{=html}\n<div class=\"leaflet html-widget html-fill-item\" id=\"htmlwidget-af34caf5b50f2d6f8e71\" style=\"width:100%;height:464px;\"></div>\n<script type=\"application/json\" data-for=\"htmlwidget-af34caf5b50f2d6f8e71\">{\"x\":{\"options\":{\"crs\":{\"crsClass\":\"L.CRS.EPSG3857\",\"code\":null,\"proj4def\":null,\"projectedBounds\":null,\"options\":{}}},\"calls\":[{\"method\":\"addProviderTiles\",\"args\":[\"OpenStreetMap\",null,\"OSM\",{\"errorTileUrl\":\"\",\"noWrap\":false,\"detectRetina\":false}]},{\"method\":\"addProviderTiles\",\"args\":[\"Esri.WorldImagery\",null,\"Satellite\",{\"errorTileUrl\":\"\",\"noWrap\":false,\"detectRetina\":false}]},{\"method\":\"createMapPane\",\"args\":[\"polygon\",420]},{\"method\":\"addPolygons\",\"args\":[[[[{\"lng\":[5.930063995452003,6.000084129232034,6.00024083941382,5.930286357864063,5.930063995452003],\"lat\":[50.19377293504808,50.193